<section class="text-size-">
  <h2 data-toc-exclude>Finding elements by user-facing attributes</h2>

  <div class="mt-200r fragment">
    <p>
      Playwright recommends prioritizing locators based on
      <strong>user-facing attributes</strong>
    </p>
    <div class="fragment">
      <ul class="mt-100r">
        <li>
          <if-nodepw><code>page.getByRole()</code></if-nodepw>
          <if-pypw><code>page.get_by_role()</code></if-pypw>
          to locate interactive elements like
          <code>button</code>, <code>a</code>, <code>input</code>, etc.
        </li>
        <li>
          <if-nodepw><code>page.getByLabel()</code></if-nodepw>
          <if-pypw><code>page.get_by_label()</code></if-pypw>
          to locate form fields</li>
        <li>
          <if-nodepw><code>page.getByPlaceholder()</code></if-nodepw>
          <if-pypw><code>page.get_by_placeholder()</code></if-pypw>
          to locate form fields without a label and having a placeholder text
        </li>
        <li>
          <if-nodepw><code>page.getByText()</code></if-nodepw>
          <if-pypw><code>page.get_by_text()</code></if-pypw>
          to find non interactive elements like
          <code>div</code>, <code>span</code>, <code>p</code>, etc.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-200r smaller">
        See examples:
        <if-nodepw><a>https://playwright.dev/docs/locators</a></if-nodepw>
        <if-pypw><a>https://playwright.dev/python/docs/locators</a></if-pypw>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
